    {
      "coptic": "ⲛⲧⲉⲣⲉⲡⲡⲉⲧⲟⲩⲁⲁⲃ ⲇⲉ ⲁⲡⲁ ⲡⲉⲥⲩⲛⲑⲓⲟⲥ · ⲣⲟⲩϩⲃⲇⲟⲙⲁⲥ ⲉϥϣⲱⲛⲉ · ⲙⲡⲉⲛⲉⲥⲛⲏⲩ ϣⲓⲛⲉ ⲛⲥⲱϥ · ⲉϥⲙⲉⲉⲩⲉ ϫⲉⲉϥϩⲙⲡ**ⲃⲏⲃ** ·",
      "english": "Now when the holy man Apa Pisentius had been sick. for a whole week, and the brethren had made no enquiries after him, for they thought he was in a cave,",
      "source": "Life of Pisentius part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.pisentius.budge:1-31",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲡⲉϫⲉ ⲓⲏⲥⲟⲩⲥ ⲛⲁϥ ⲛⲓⲃⲁϣⲟⲣ ⲟⲩⲟⲛⲧⲟⲩ **ⲃⲏⲃ** ⲙⲙⲁⲩ ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲛⲓϩⲁⲗⲁϯ ⲛⲧⲉⲧⲫⲉ ⲟⲩⲟⲛⲧⲟⲩ ⲙⲁⲛⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲡϣⲏⲣⲓ ⲇⲉ ⲛⲑⲟϥ ⲙⲫⲣⲱⲙⲓ ⲙⲙⲟⲛⲧⲉϥ ⲙⲁⲛⲣⲉⲕϫⲱϥ ⲉⲣⲟϥ .",
      "english": "Jesus said to him, 'The foxes have holes, and the birds of the sky have nests, but the Son of Man has nowhere to lay his head.'",
      "source": "01_Matthew_08",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:nt.matt.bohairic:08",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲕⲁⲓ ⲅⲁⲣ ⲛⲁⲛⲟⲩⲥ · ⲉⲕϩⲛⲧⲙⲏⲏⲧⲉ ⲛⲟⲩϣⲟ ϩⲛⲑⲃⲃⲓⲟ ⲛⲓⲙ ⲛϩⲟⲩⲟ ⲉⲟⲩⲁ ⲉϥϩⲛⲟⲩ**ⲃⲏⲃ** ⲛϩⲟⲉⲓⲧⲉ · ⲉϥϣⲟⲟⲡ ϩⲛⲟⲩⲙⲛⲧϫⲁⲥⲓϩⲏⲧ ·",
      "english": "For it is very much better for thee to be one among a crowd of a thousand people and to possess a very little humility, than to be a man living in the cave of a hyena in pride.",
      "source": "Instructions of Apa Pachomius in MERC.AR in Budge ed. - part 2",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pachomius.instructions.budge:35-69",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
